{"seq":2,"at":"2026-10-20","kind":"edited","target":{"type":"article","id":"a0629"},"reason":"Rewritten by the merge to take in the printed cards' questions.","by":"merge sport-games/football","ref":"quiz-archive/runs/tp-ingest/decisions/sport-games__football.g2.json","changes":[{"field":"bodyEn","diff":[["=",94],["-","team."],["+","team – and one of them was even handed out by the English."],["=",881],["+","Not every famous nickname was coined at home. Robert Huth, born in Berlin on 18 August 1984, left the youth team of 1. FC Union Berlin for Chelsea at sixteen and spent his entire professional career in England, winning the league with Chelsea in 2005 and 2006 and, sensationally, with Leicester City in 2016. A towering, uncompromising centre-back who also won 19 caps for Germany, he was christened \"The Berlin Wall\" by English fans – a joke on his birthplace and on how hard he was to get past.\n\n"],["=",123],["+","\n| The Berlin Wall | Robert Huth | Leicester City |"]]},{"field":"bodyDe","diff":[["=",78],["-","Nationalmannschaft."],["+","Nationalmannschaft – und einen davon vergaben sogar die Engländer."],["=",823],["+","Nicht jeder berühmte Spitzname entstand in der Heimat. Robert Huth, geboren am 18. August 1984 in Berlin, wechselte mit sechzehn aus der Jugend des 1. FC Union Berlin zum FC Chelsea und verbrachte seine gesamte Profikarriere in England: Mit Chelsea wurde er 2005 und 2006 Meister, mit Leicester City 2016 sensationell ein drittes Mal. Der baumlange, kompromisslose Innenverteidiger, der auch 19 Länderspiele für Deutschland bestritt, wurde von den englischen Fans „The Berlin Wall“ getauft – ein Wortspiel mit seiner Geburtsstadt und damit, wie schwer an ihm vorbeizukommen war.\n\n"],["=",125],["+","\n| The Berlin Wall | Robert Huth | Leicester City |"]]}]},
